' Pre-execution acceptance of one offered-funded candidate (DR-64, decision D1).
' The producer and every validator run the same check from the signed envelope
' and the original root R0, before any runtime entry. The signed phloLimit is the
' P1 safety margin: the unprovable remainder is held in full, or the candidate is
' rejected with no effect and no charge.
'
' Source of truth: docs/casper/theory/cost-accounting-decision-records.md (DR-64);
'                  publications/cost-accounting/cost-accounted-rho.tex
'                  (sec:acceptance-protocol, thm:decidability, def:conservative-demand).
' Palette:  input = supply blue · static analysis = process lilac · funding gate = teal
'           execution = pool green · settlement/refund = note green · reject = red
'           decisions = control amber
' Render:  plantuml -tsvg docs/casper/theory/diagrams/offered-preexecution-acceptance.puml
'          (or: ./render.sh offered-preexecution-acceptance.puml)

@startuml offered-preexecution-acceptance
!include palette.iuml
$ca_base_skin()
skinparam ArrowColor $ca_neutral
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #333333
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor $ca_control
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor #333333
title Pre-execution acceptance of an offered-funded candidate (DR-64)

start
:signed offered envelope\nand original root <latex>R_0</latex>; <<$ca_supply>>
:resolve lexical names\nfrom the envelope seed; <<$ca_process>>
:static_authority_plan\nfor each signature lane <latex>s</latex>; <<$ca_process>>
if (lane demand provable?) then (yes)
  :<latex>\Delta^{\mathrm{known}}_s</latex> = exact lane demand\nplus syntactic byte charges; <<$ca_process>>
else (no · UnprovableDemand)
  :<latex>\Delta^{\mathrm{known}}_s = 0</latex>\n(the remainder covers the lane); <<$ca_process>>
endif
:<latex>R = \left(\mathrm{phloLimit} - \sum_s \Delta^{\mathrm{known}}_s\right)\cdot \mathrm{phloPrice}</latex>; <<$ca_delta>>
:fit known holds plus the complete remainder <latex>R</latex>\non eligible signed sources at <latex>R_0</latex>\n(hold_cap, debit_cap, total exposure); <<$ca_gate>>
if (holds fit the supply at <latex>R_0</latex>?) then (no)
  :reject before any runtime entry\nno effect · no charge; <<$ca_rejectfill>>
  note right $ca_note_red
    P1 acceptance step 5: the deployment is
    rejected without executing any part of it.
    DR-72 quarantines it with a status entry.
  end note
  stop
else (yes · resources committed)
  :execute in a fresh offered runtime\nresource_bound = known + remainder; <<$ca_pool>>
  if (meter outcome) then (within bounds)
    :charge measured use · refund unused hold\nto the original sources; <<$ca_note_green>>
  elseif (signed limit exhausted\nin a capped part) then
    :classified user failure: roll back,\nkeep billable prefix and fee, refund rest; <<$ca_note_amber>>
  else (exact lane overrun)
    :correctness failure: reject candidate,\nrestore pre-state, no charge; <<$ca_rejectfill>>
  endif
endif
stop

legend bottom
  |= colour |= meaning |
  |<$ca_supply>| signed input and authenticated root |
  |<$ca_process>| static demand analysis (existing analyzers) |
  |<$ca_delta>| signed-limit remainder (P1 safety margin) |
  |<$ca_gate>| funding gate before execution |
  |<$ca_pool>| execution with committed resources |
  |<$ca_note_green>| settlement and refund |
  |<$ca_note_amber>| classified user failure |
  |<$ca_rejectfill>| rejection or correctness failure (no charge) |
  |<$ca_control>| decision |
endlegend

@enduml
